    "RFC2545-3-2": {
      "note": "Independently rejudged against RFC2545 Section 3's length 16 for a global alone and 32 when the link-local is included; direct construction writes the selected 16/32 length and corresponding ordered bytes, and replay reconstructs the entire NextHopHex field rather than reducing it to one address; current compatibility and live/stored replay fixtures assert literal complete wire encodings including length 0x20, while global-only and invalid-width controls in the existing writer/policy composition prevent an arbitrary legal-looking address or malformed width from satisfying the rule; the changed checkRFC2545NextHops uses the actual selected IPv6 session and topology-owned Ze global/link-local, requires exact decoded one-versus-two address shapes for off-link/on-link routes, and separately reads route installation, not dataplane forwarding; the strengthened topology does not weaken any width assertion; mapped single fields, standalone negotiated link-local and RD-bearing VPN fields remain explicitly separate family/draft contracts; current native bindings and Main-observed functional evidence complement the source judgment rather than deriving it from passing names",
      "requirement_sha": "b5d1c52dd182fc35",
